; The one variable: where a CSGMesh3D's `mesh` comes from. A `.tres` ArrayMesh, a `.tres`
; BoxMesh and an inline ArrayMesh each build the brush from the mesh's surfaces, and each
; face takes the node's `material`, else its surface's own (csg_shape.cpp:1168-1172). So the
; first, fourth and boolean pairs read red and green, the second blue, and the box yellow.
; unit-csg-mesh holds only inline PrimitiveMeshes under a node `material`.
